            0.371
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.4 An Exploration in Rectangles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.385,
            0.734,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": "Construct a rectangle ABCD with AB = 7 cm and BC = 4 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.408,
            0.836,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "Imagine X to be a point that can be moved anywhere along the side AD. Similarly, imagine Y to be a point that can be moved anywhere along the side BC. Note that X can also be placed on the end point A or D. Similarly, Y can also be placed on the end point B or C."
        },
